          "name": "Grafana Get Data Source Cache Config",
          "request": {
            "name": "Grafana Get Data Source Cache Config",
            "description": {
              "content": "Retrieves the caching configuration settings for a specific data source in Grafana identified by its unique identifier (dataSourceUID). This GET operation allows administrators and users with appropriate permissions to view the current cache configuration parameters associated with a particular data source, which may include settings such as cache TTL (time-to-live), cache size limits, and enabled/disabled status. The response provides insight into how query results from this data source are being cached to optimize performance and reduce load on the underlying data source system.",
